# declared-fake.env: the DECLARED FAKE half of gate 7's secret-scan fixture.
#
# Ticket: ORI-T-0016.  Spec: spec/CI_CD.md section 1 gate 7,
# spec/ENV_SETUP.md section 4, spec/TESTING.md section 5.
# Proof: ops/gates/gate-7.md.  Rule: AICD section 14.
#
# Every line below carries a string that matches one of the patterns in
# scripts/secret-scan.sh, and every one of them carries the
# declared-fake marker INSIDE THE VALUE. The scan must find all of them and
# exempt all of them, which is why this file is tracked rather than generated:
# it is the input that proves the exemption path runs, and a run that exempts
# nothing is a run where the fixture has gone missing.
#
# prove.sh derives the CAUGHT half from this file by replacing the marker with
# eleven other characters, which leaves every value the same shape and the same
# length and leaves none of them declared. That derived file exists only in a
# temporary directory inside a throwaway git repository: a tracked file holding
# an undeclared secret-shaped string is the thing this gate exists to reject,
# so this fixture ships the declared form and manufactures the other one.
#
# prove.sh also wraps both forms in NUL bytes, to build the files the scanner
# used to skip, and bakes the derived form into a 16 MiB binary. Those are
# manufactured from this file for the same reason: one sample, one place to
# change, and nothing undeclared at rest anywhere.
#
# THE FILE prove.sh BUILDS FROM THIS ONE IS ascii-in-nul-bytes.bin. It is ASCII
# between NUL bytes behind a JKS magic number, which is the shape a compiled
# object and a SQLite file have. It was called keystore.p12 and was neither; a
# real .p12 and a real Java keystore encrypt the key, so the scanner reports
# exit 0 on them with the key inside. Both were built and measured, and the
# output is in ops/gates/gate-7.md.
#
# AND THE SCANNER THIS FILE FEEDS IS NOT A GATE. Gate 7's secret scan is not
# installed: escalation E-0003. Nothing here may be cited as protection.
#
# The names on the left are from the secrets inventory in spec/ENV_SETUP.md
# section 4. The values authenticate nothing anywhere.

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIAFIXTUREFAKE00000
VCS_APP_TOKEN=ghp_FIXTUREFAKE0000000000000000000000000
PROVIDER_ORI_API_KEY=sk-ant-FIXTUREFAKE00000000000000000
NOTIFY_SLACK_SECRET=xoxb-FIXTUREFAKE-000000000000
VCS_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN FIXTUREFAKE PRIVATE KEY-----"
ENGINE_CLIENT_TOKEN=FIXTUREFAKE000000000

